WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:07.800
Alright, so I just found the example, so you can see we have the Fair Valley gap here.

00:07.800 --> 00:12.800
And price created this high inside the Fair Valley gap.

00:12.800 --> 00:19.160
And we also have this Fair Valley gap.

00:19.160 --> 00:22.600
Price came into this Fair Valley gap, right created this low here.

00:22.600 --> 00:24.400
So what happens then?

00:24.400 --> 00:28.880
Price takes out the high that was formed inside the Fair Valley gap.

00:28.880 --> 00:35.920
And then it goes to the low that was formed inside the Fair Valley gap.

00:35.920 --> 00:43.240
So this is like, I think one of the best ways to find your daily buys or actually you can

00:43.240 --> 00:50.400
use it as a trading model itself, but I wouldn't suggest it.

00:50.400 --> 00:56.820
So over here you can also see that we have another Fair Valley gap, right?

00:56.820 --> 01:00.060
And this high was formed inside this Fair Valley gap.

01:00.060 --> 01:02.500
So price takes out the high.

01:02.500 --> 01:10.660
And then you can see that we have this Fair Valley gap as well, right?

01:10.660 --> 01:15.820
And this low was formed inside the Fair Valley gap right here.

01:15.820 --> 01:21.340
So price takes out the high that was formed inside this Fair Valley gap.

01:21.340 --> 01:28.740
And then it goes towards the low that was formed inside this tiny Fair Valley gap.

01:28.740 --> 01:34.780
So you can use it as I say before to find your daily buys or a model itself.

01:34.780 --> 01:39.940
So I hope by now it is clear and just wanted to make a very short video about this because

01:39.940 --> 01:45.260
this is very easy and it is very, very effective.

01:45.260 --> 01:48.020
Remember it only works with Fair Valley gaps.

01:49.020 --> 01:56.660
And also one thing to note is that let's say price comes into the Fair Valley gap, right?

01:56.660 --> 02:01.820
And as soon as it comes and creates a high and then the high gets purged, then you don't

02:01.820 --> 02:06.180
have to look for anything that Fair Valley gaps becomes invalid.

02:06.180 --> 02:10.220
Only one high is allowed in one Fair Valley gap.

02:10.220 --> 02:14.820
If there are two highs that Fair Valley gap is invalid, okay?

02:14.820 --> 02:20.660
So for example, this is another high that is created inside this Fair Valley gap, right?

02:20.660 --> 02:22.620
And it took out the first high.

02:22.620 --> 02:25.940
Now I will not be looking at this because the job is done here.

02:25.940 --> 02:31.740
So I will move on and look to find another setup.

02:31.740 --> 02:37.740
If there's one high like this, then that liquidity pool is valid.

02:37.740 --> 02:40.340
So yeah, that's what I wanted to tell you.

02:40.340 --> 02:42.340
So let's move on to next chapter.

